Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:38:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] vd_lavc: hold back 4 hardware decoded frames instead of 2

With 2 frames, 31 Mbps 4K AV1 at 2x speed still was dropping frames.
Make the queue 4, which nicelly hides decoder latency.

Note that the main issue comes from that not every frame is decoded in
the same time for those AV1 samples, so we need to eat the latency
spikes. And also it's good for pipelining with rendering.

(cherry picked from commit 55d3feb45c3dda1afd02b3087d3463c57d6514f7)
---
 video/decode/vd_lavc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
index 3b4fd2f..674db3d 100644
--- a/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
+++ b/video/decode/vd_lavc.c
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@ static enum AVPixelFormat get_format_hwdec(struct AVCodecContext *avctx,
 static int hwdec_opt_help(struct mp_log *log, const m_option_t *opt,
                           struct bstr name);
 
-#define HWDEC_DELAY_QUEUE_COUNT 2
+#define HWDEC_DELAY_QUEUE_COUNT 4
 
 #define OPT_BASE_STRUCT struct vd_lavc_params
 
